('e74a0578-acaa-5fa0-a8ce-7e7185b8559a','02bf2dbe-0f31-51f5-a961-59c4072b4d75',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the feeling of being very worried about something','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'اضطراب، نگرانی، دل‌شوره',array['concern']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['great/considerable anxiety Then began a day of great anxiety.','acute/deep/high anxiety The patient''s panic attacks are caused by acute anxiety.','constant anxiety She lives a life of constant anxiety over money and job security.','increasing/mounting anxiety There is mounting anxiety about the rise in violent crime.','public anxiety the wave of public anxiety about food safety','cause/create/lead to anxiety Their nuclear programme is causing mounting anxiety among other nations, especially Israel.','arouse/provoke anxiety (= cause it ) The presence of Indian troops near the border has aroused considerable anxiety in neighbouring Pakistan.','feel/suffer from anxiety The child may feel anxiety about being away from home.','reduce/relieve anxiety The drug helps to reduce anxiety, allowing you to feel relaxed.','a source of anxiety For many people, the primary source of anxiety is work.','somebody''s level of anxiety Patients experience high levels of anxiety at time of admission to hospital.','feelings of anxiety Having an operation naturally entails feelings of anxiety.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There is considerable anxiety among staff about job losses.","translation":"نگرانی قابل توجهی در بین کارکنان در مورد از دست دادن شغل وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000942527.mp3"},{"sentence":"There is growing public anxiety over levels of air pollution in our cities.","translation":"نگرانی عمومی در مورد میزان آلودگی هوا در شهرهای ما رو به افزایش است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647027.mp3"},{"sentence":"The fear of unemployment can be a source of deep anxiety to people.","translation":"ترس از بیکاری می تواند منبعی برای نگرانی عمیق مردم باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647030.mp3"},{"sentence":"his feelings of anxiety","translation":"احساس اضطراب او","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647031.mp3"},{"sentence":"A high level of anxiety was created by the introduction of cameras into the factory.","translation":"سطح بالایی از اضطراب با ورود دوربین ها به کارخانه ایجاد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647032.mp3"},{"sentence":"It can help if you discuss your anxieties with someone.","translation":"اگر نگرانی های خود را با کسی در میان بگذارید، می تواند کمک کننده باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647034.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('dc6d8f19-dc31-53ad-ac69-47c665e26743','02bf2dbe-0f31-51f5-a961-59c4072b4d75',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a feeling of wanting to do something very much','[ uncountable ]',null,'احساس تمایل زیاد برای انجام کاری','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['great/considerable anxiety Then began a day of great anxiety.','acute/deep/high anxiety The patient''s panic attacks are caused by acute anxiety.','constant anxiety She lives a life of constant anxiety over money and job security.','increasing/mounting anxiety There is mounting anxiety about the rise in violent crime.','public anxiety the wave of public anxiety about food safety','cause/create/lead to anxiety Their nuclear programme is causing mounting anxiety among other nations, especially Israel.','arouse/provoke anxiety (= cause it ) The presence of Indian troops near the border has aroused considerable anxiety in neighbouring Pakistan.','feel/suffer from anxiety The child may feel anxiety about being away from home.','reduce/relieve anxiety The drug helps to reduce anxiety, allowing you to feel relaxed.','a source of anxiety For many people, the primary source of anxiety is work.','somebody''s level of anxiety Patients experience high levels of anxiety at time of admission to hospital.','feelings of anxiety Having an operation naturally entails feelings of anxiety.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I nearly fell in my anxiety to get downstairs quickly.","translation":"تقریباً در اضطراب افتادم که سریع از پله ها پایین بیایم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647037.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('4f9f440e-c1b0-5888-81d0-781efe5e933e','3481bf8b-822f-5b9d-b07a-e140db0fe42b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','worried about something',null,null,'نگران، مضطرب','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He was a bit anxious about the safety of the machinery.","translation":"او کمی نگران ایمنی ماشین آلات بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000942552.mp3"},{"sentence":"We were anxious for you.","translation":"ما دلواپس تو بودیم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647040.mp3"},{"sentence":"She was anxious that it might be cancer.","translation":"او نگران بود که ممکن است سرطان باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000942559.mp3"},{"sentence":"She gave me an anxious look.","translation":"نگاهی مضطرب به من انداخت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000942556.mp3"},{"sentence":"She is anxious about the interview.","translation":"او در مورد مصاحبه مضطرب است.","audio_url":null},{"sentence":"They are anxious for their son.","translation":"آنها نگران پسرشان هستند.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,6),
('7dda4a6f-a8ff-5fa6-9937-8f809882d0b3','3481bf8b-822f-5b9d-b07a-e140db0fe42b',2,null,null,'spoken & written','an anxious time or situation is one in which you feel nervous or worried',null,null,'زمان یا موقعیت مضطرب زمانی است که در آن احساس عصبی یا نگرانی می کنید',array['worrying']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We had an anxious couple of weeks waiting for the test results.","translation":"چند هفته مضطرب منتظر نتایج آزمایش بودیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000942563.mp3"},{"sentence":"There was an anxious moment when the plane suddenly dropped.","translation":"لحظه ای مضطرب بود که هواپیما ناگهان سقوط کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647043.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('b5c63143-36eb-5a20-ad81-ed0090c58ac5','3481bf8b-822f-5b9d-b07a-e140db0fe42b',3,null,null,'spoken & written','feeling strongly that you want to do something or want something to happen',null,null,'به شدت احساس می کنید که می خواهید کاری را انجام دهید یا می خواهید چیزی اتفاق بیفتد',array['keen']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The company is anxious to improve its image.","translation":"این شرکت مشتاق بهبود تصویر خود است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000942569.mp3"},{"sentence":"He seemed most anxious to speak to me alone.","translation":"به نظر می رسید که او بیش از همه مشتاق بود که به تنهایی با من صحبت کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647046.mp3"},{"sentence":"The president is anxious not to have another crisis.","translation":"رئیس جمهور نگران است که بحران دیگری نداشته باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647050.mp3"},{"sentence":"Why was she so anxious for me to stay?","translation":"چرا او اینقدر نگران بود که من بمانم؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647053.mp3"},{"sentence":"We were all anxious for news.","translation":"همه ما مشتاق خبری بودیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647056.mp3"},{"sentence":"Both sides were anxious that the agreement should be signed as quickly as possible.","translation":"هر دو طرف نگران بودند که توافقنامه باید هر چه سریعتر امضا شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647059.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('56f2de0f-dbf7-50f3-bba4-53724ad1dd89','6d72840f-9b15-5a78-badf-aabb677083ab',1,null,null,'spoken & written','anyone',null,null,'هر کس، کسی (در پرسش و نفی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('83209c30-eaa4-5d0c-9f33-df5c050a3a3b','83760842-a44f-5f0c-9b6f-6532afac54e4',1,null,null,'spoken & written','something that you say or write to show that you are sorry for doing something wrong','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'عذرخواهی، پوزش','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make an apology I hope you are going to make an apology.','issue an apology (= make an official public apology ) The company issued an official apology for the incident.','get/receive an apology He received a formal apology from the company.','offer an apology We would like to offer our sincere apologies for the delay.','accept somebody’s apology Please accept my apologies for having to cancel our meeting.','demand an apology China continued to demand a full apology from the US.','owe somebody an apology I’m afraid I owe you an apology.','publish an apology (= print it in a newspaper ) The newspaper group was forced to publish a full apology.','mumble/mutter an apology (= say it quietly, especially because you are embarrassed ) He bumped into me and mumbled an apology.','my sincere/profound apologies (= used when you feel very sorry ) Firstly, my sincere apologies for not having contacted you earlier. ‘I have been guilty of making some insensitive remarks, ’ said Wright, who offered his profound apologies to everyone concerned.','a public apology The authorities published a public apology in the newspaper.','a formal apology Russia is demanding a formal apology.','an official apology The company has made an official apology and is offering compensation.','a written apology The police sent a written apology to the family.','a full apology The prime minister made a full apology in the House of Commons.','an abject apology formal (= one that shows that you are very sorry ) The BBC issued an abject apology for insulting the Queen.','profuse apologies formal (= when someone says that they are sorry several times ) Moira telephoned with profuse apologies for the misunderstanding.','a letter of apology We agreed to write a letter of apology.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The minister had to issue a formal public apology for his remarks.","translation":"وزیر مجبور شد به دلیل اظهارات خود عذرخواهی رسمی عمومی کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000079.mp3"},{"sentence":"She finally received an apology from the company.","translation":"او در نهایت یک عذرخواهی از شرکت دریافت کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001647324.mp3"},{"sentence":"an apology to passengers for any inconvenience caused","translation":"عذرخواهی از مسافران برای هر گونه ناراحتی ایجاد شده است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000080.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('cdb4e7e8-7fc9-5d19-99ec-1835990b7073','83760842-a44f-5f0c-9b6f-6532afac54e4',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'apologies','عذرخواهی، پوزش','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make an apology I hope you are going to make an apology.','issue an apology (= make an official public apology ) The company issued an official apology for the incident.','get/receive an apology He received a formal apology from the company.','offer an apology We would like to offer our sincere apologies for the delay.','accept somebody’s apology Please accept my apologies for having to cancel our meeting.','demand an apology China continued to demand a full apology from the US.','owe somebody an apology I’m afraid I owe you an apology.','publish an apology (= print it in a newspaper ) The newspaper group was forced to publish a full apology.','mumble/mutter an apology (= say it quietly, especially because you are embarrassed ) He bumped into me and mumbled an apology.','my sincere/profound apologies (= used when you feel very sorry ) Firstly, my sincere apologies for not having contacted you earlier. ‘I have been guilty of making some insensitive remarks, ’ said Wright, who offered his profound apologies to everyone concerned.','a public apology The authorities published a public apology in the newspaper.','a formal apology Russia is demanding a formal apology.','an official apology The company has made an official apology and is offering compensation.','a written apology The police sent a written apology to the family.','a full apology The prime minister made a full apology in the House of Commons.','an abject apology formal (= one that shows that you are very sorry ) The BBC issued an abject apology for insulting the Queen.','profuse apologies formal (= when someone says that they are sorry several times ) Moira telephoned with profuse apologies for the misunderstanding.','a letter of apology We agreed to write a letter of apology.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
