('01985dcf-248d-5cd2-9049-d26cd78b81dd','6adcf49b-961c-5312-a1b5-dc0dbfcc3ab6',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the typical weather conditions in a particular area','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'اقلیم، آب‌وهوای یک منطقه؛ جوّ (عمومی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['warm/hot Many people prefer to live where the climate is warm.','cold/cool Scotland''s climate is too cold for these plants to survive.','mild (= not too hot and not too cold ) The region''s climate is mild all the year round.','dry She loves the dry climate of southern California.','wet/damp A damp climate can damage buildings.','humid (= with hot and wet air ) Tropical vegetation flourishes in this humid climate.','harsh ( also inhospitable formal ) (= uncomfortable and difficult to live in ) The climate of the Siberian steppes is harsh.','extreme/severe These mountain people are used to the extreme climate.','arid (= very dry ) Very few plants can flourish in such an arid climate.','temperate (= never very hot or very cold ) Europe''s climate is temperate.','tropical (= very hot and wet ) the tropical climate of Brazil','a Mediterranean climate (= typical of the areas around the Mediterranean Sea ) Croatia enjoys a Mediterranean climate.','the global/world climate (= the weather of the world ) Scientists are assessing the impact of carbon dioxide on the global climate.','a changing climate A changing climate will bring rising tides.','climate change (= a permanent change in weather conditions ) The world must reduce the emissions that cause climate change.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Los Angeles’ warm dry climate","translation":"آب و هوای گرم و خشک لس آنجلس","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000866484.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('fa9df25f-9d53-57db-8937-23dbc2c733a1','6adcf49b-961c-5312-a1b5-dc0dbfcc3ab6',2,null,null,'spoken & written','an area with particular weather conditions','[ countable ]',null,'منطقه ای با شرایط آب و هوایی خاص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['warm/hot Many people prefer to live where the climate is warm.','cold/cool Scotland''s climate is too cold for these plants to survive.','mild (= not too hot and not too cold ) The region''s climate is mild all the year round.','dry She loves the dry climate of southern California.','wet/damp A damp climate can damage buildings.','humid (= with hot and wet air ) Tropical vegetation flourishes in this humid climate.','harsh ( also inhospitable formal ) (= uncomfortable and difficult to live in ) The climate of the Siberian steppes is harsh.','extreme/severe These mountain people are used to the extreme climate.','arid (= very dry ) Very few plants can flourish in such an arid climate.','temperate (= never very hot or very cold ) Europe''s climate is temperate.','tropical (= very hot and wet ) the tropical climate of Brazil','a Mediterranean climate (= typical of the areas around the Mediterranean Sea ) Croatia enjoys a Mediterranean climate.','the global/world climate (= the weather of the world ) Scientists are assessing the impact of carbon dioxide on the global climate.','a changing climate A changing climate will bring rising tides.','climate change (= a permanent change in weather conditions ) The world must reduce the emissions that cause climate change.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"These flowers will not grow in cold climates.","translation":"این گل ها در آب و هوای سرد رشد نمی کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000866488.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('ead24429-d93f-5884-8b66-acea6243b41a','6adcf49b-961c-5312-a1b5-dc0dbfcc3ab6',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the general feeling or situation in a place at a particular time','[ countable usually singular ]',null,'احساس یا موقعیت کلی در یک مکان در یک زمان خاص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Small businesses are finding it hard to survive in the present economic climate.","translation":"بقای کسب و کارهای کوچک در شرایط اقتصادی کنونی دشوار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000866477.mp3"},{"sentence":"a climate of growing racial intolerance in large cities","translation":"فضای رشد عدم تحمل نژادی در شهرهای بزرگ","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000866480.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('2563cfb3-e29f-578c-bd56-94e2b79402c1','243e8bc6-feab-5bd0-8dee-e5cb6dd5ea65',1,null,null,'spoken & written','very carefully',null,null,'به‌دقت، موشکافانه؛ نزدیک‌به‌نزدیک','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The detective watched him closely , waiting for a reply.","translation":"کارآگاه او را از نزدیک زیر نظر گرفت و منتظر پاسخ بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001686795.mp3"},{"sentence":"Political activity is closely controlled.","translation":"فعالیت سیاسی به شدت کنترل می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001686801.mp3"},{"sentence":"Details of the program are a closely-guarded secret .","translation":"جزئیات برنامه یک راز کاملاً محافظت شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001686802.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('90dc1890-e8a3-5bf9-8fc7-d99ec5fc0449','243e8bc6-feab-5bd0-8dee-e5cb6dd5ea65',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to a very great degree',null,null,'به درجه بسیار عالی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I have been closely involved in the work of both committees.","translation":"من از نزدیک درگیر کار هر دو کمیته بوده ام.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001686809.mp3"},{"sentence":"The successful applicant will be working closely with our international staff.","translation":"متقاضی موفق از نزدیک با کارکنان بین المللی ما همکاری خواهد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001686813.mp3"},{"sentence":"a creature that closely resembles a red monkey","translation":"موجودی که شباهت زیادی به میمون قرمز دارد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001686817.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('93cc8d65-c0a0-58f5-a201-4609c1564691','243e8bc6-feab-5bd0-8dee-e5cb6dd5ea65',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'closely related/connected/associated etc','به‌دقت، موشکافانه؛ نزدیک‌به‌نزدیک','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('2b4203fc-92a1-5e15-ab56-5e90abb54740','243e8bc6-feab-5bd0-8dee-e5cb6dd5ea65',4,null,null,'spoken & written','in a way that is close to other things in time or space',null,null,'به گونه ای که در زمان یا مکان به چیزهای دیگر نزدیک باشد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"lightning, followed closely by thunder","translation":"رعد و برق همراه با رعد و برق","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000867468.mp3"},{"sentence":"We were so closely packed in the elevator I could hardly move.","translation":"آنقدر در آسانسور جمع شده بودیم که به سختی می توانستیم حرکت کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000867469.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('1a66d19b-b61a-5bb8-b4d2-3fd022636e9d','78424461-6ff9-56c2-b914-063b44793fcc',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the things that people wear to cover their body or keep warm',null,'a change of clothes , → plain-clothes','لباس، پوشاک','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['wear clothes She always wears beautiful clothes.','be dressed in … clothes The man was dressed in ordinary clothes.','put your clothes on I told him to get up and put some clothes on.','take off/remove your clothes She took off her clothes and slipped into bed.','change your clothes I usually change my clothes as soon as I get home from work.','a change of clothes He only took a small bag with a change of clothes.','warm clothes If you’re walking in the mountains, take plenty of warm clothes.','casual clothes Most people feel more comfortable in casual clothes.','evening clothes I don’t often have a chance to wear formal evening clothes.','designer clothes (= made by a well-known designer ) She spends hundreds of pounds on designer clothes.','somebody’s best clothes They wore their best clothes for the photograph.','formal clothes It’s best to wear formal clothes for an interview.','school/work clothes Work clothes tend to be black, blue, or grey.','sports clothes Lou was wearing sports clothes and sunglasses.','ordinary/everyday clothes Everyone else was wearing ordinary clothes.','civilian clothes (= ordinary clothes rather than a military uniform ) a US army lieutenant in civilian clothes','baby clothes a shop for baby clothes','maternity clothes (= for women who are having a baby )','winter/summer clothes The shops are already full of winter clothes.','plain clothes (= ordinary clothes that the police wear in order not to be recognized ) He was arrested by officers in plain clothes.','clean clothes I had no clean clothes.','dry clothes You’d better change into dry clothes or you’ll get cold.','fashionable/trendy clothes The club was full of beautiful people wearing trendy clothes.','elegant Italian people are often admired for their elegant clothes.','old-fashioned I decided to throw out all my old-fashioned clothes.','smart British English Do you have to wear smart clothes to work?','scruffy (= dirty and untidy ) She was poor and dressed in scruffy clothes.','second-hand clothes (= not new ) Charity shops sell second-hand clothes at low prices.','dowdy (= unfashionable and unattractive ) Dowdy clothes make you have less confidence in yourself.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"What sort of clothes was he wearing?","translation":"چه لباسی پوشیده بود؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001686883.mp3"},{"sentence":"I showered and put on clean clothes.","translation":"دوش گرفتم و لباس تمیز پوشیدم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001686893.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was still in his work clothes.","translation":"او هنوز در لباس کارش بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000330.mp3"},{"sentence":"a clothes shop","translation":"یک مغازه لباس فروشی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001686898.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('2ad0c3eb-c084-5801-a9e0-3e4dbd18419a','5a08f2d5-9c06-557c-a64c-08ced91b4e47',1,'bring together','گرد هم بیاورند','spoken & written','to get things of the same type from different places and bring them together','[ transitive ]',null,'جمع‌آوری کردن؛ آوردن (چند نقطه از یک)؛ جمع کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"After 25 years of collecting recipes, she has compiled them into a cookbook.","translation":"پس از 25 سال جمع آوری دستور العمل ها، او آنها را در یک کتاب آشپزی گردآوری کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001087926.mp3"},{"sentence":"The company collects information about consumer trends.","translation":"این شرکت اطلاعاتی در مورد روند مصرف کنندگان جمع آوری می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001087927.mp3"},{"sentence":"We’ve been out collecting signatures for our petition.","translation":"ما در حال جمع آوری امضا برای طومار خود بوده ایم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001680405.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
