('a63c324d-7edb-53e7-9077-e32460d7baf3','0998769c-7761-57ef-9e23-029d6ffe09fe',8,null,null,'spoken & written','an action that tries to prevent something bad from happening, or an argument that is used to prove that something is wrong',null,null,'عملی که سعی می‌کند از اتفاق بدی جلوگیری کند، یا استدلالی که برای اثبات اشتباه بودن چیزی به کار می‌رود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The road blocks were a counter to terrorist attacks in that area.","translation":"بلوک های جاده مقابله با حملات تروریستی در آن منطقه بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001113970.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('050ad7d9-e66a-5db9-b746-b627d44ce1e0','75719cf9-4ae9-5535-9f2a-9d17fc8fcdc3',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to say something in order to try to prove that what someone said was not true or as a reply to something','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'گفتن چیزی به منظور تلاش برای اثبات اینکه چیزی که کسی گفته درست نیست یا به عنوان پاسخی به چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"‘I could ask the same thing of you, ’ she countered.","translation":"او پاسخ داد: «من می‌توانم همین را از شما بپرسم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000842346.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was determined to counter the bribery allegations.","translation":"او مصمم به مقابله با اتهامات رشوه بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000842349.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('bc84f54b-d571-55fd-9499-9814be1e3ce0','75719cf9-4ae9-5535-9f2a-9d17fc8fcdc3',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to do something in order to prevent something bad from happening or to reduce its bad effects','[ transitive ]',null,'انجام کاری برای جلوگیری از وقوع یک اتفاق بد یا کاهش اثرات بد آن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Exercise helps to counter the effects of stress.","translation":"ورزش به مقابله با اثرات استرس کمک می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000842354.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('bf4d73fc-3f91-5645-b374-575d3365722c','935470c9-d18f-51e3-83f3-f686f093ba39',1,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be/run/go counter to something',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('245eb78b-4687-5896-b2d2-49a09b1345ad','840c6c63-e605-547a-abe8-3eef6ccaeab8',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the opposite of something',null,null,'برعکس چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a counterproductive thing to do (= producing results opposite to what you wanted )","translation":"یک کار معکوس برای انجام (= ایجاد نتایجی برخلاف آنچه می خواستید)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000842312.mp3"},{"sentence":"It is not hard to find a counter-example (= an example that shows the opposite ) .","translation":"یافتن مثالی متضاد (= مثالی که خلاف آن را نشان می دهد) دشوار نیست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000381.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('999143a3-6e29-5d7a-a67b-e5aa14aaa715','840c6c63-e605-547a-abe8-3eef6ccaeab8',2,null,null,'spoken & written','done or given as a reaction to something, especially to oppose it',null,null,'انجام می شود یا به عنوان واکنش به چیزی، به ویژه برای مخالفت با آن انجام می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"claims and counterclaims","translation":"دعاوی و دعاوی متقابل","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000842324.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('54ca59e1-35da-5fb2-9b28-d9ff18e6fdf5','840c6c63-e605-547a-abe8-3eef6ccaeab8',3,null,null,'spoken & written','matching something',null,null,'مطابقت دادن چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"my counterpart in the American system (= someone who has the same job as I have )","translation":"همتای من در سیستم آمریکایی (= کسی که شغلی مشابه من دارد)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000842318.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('aaf4b80d-2d4d-59bd-b81a-d5b134e769bd','0bdffdc1-ff26-5b5d-a9a0-f5ec1243344b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an area of land that is controlled by its own government, president , king etc','[ countable ]','mother country','کشور؛ سرزمین؛ حومه (منطقه روستایی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a foreign country (= not your own country ) Have you ever worked in a foreign country?','a strange country (= not your own country ) She was in a strange country, with no friends and no family.','a European/African/Asian etc country The president will be visiting four European countries.','a democratic/capitalist/communist etc country the former socialist countries of Eastern Europe','your home/native country (= where you were born or live permanently ) After five years in America, she returned to her home country, Japan.','a developing/Third World country (= poor and trying to increase its industry and trade ) Many developing countries receive some foreign aid.','a developed country (= rich and where most people have a comfortable life ) Developed countries are responsible for most emissions of carbon dioxide.','an underdeveloped country (= poor and developing more slowly than others ) The disease still exists, mainly in underdeveloped countries.','an industrialized country America and other industrialized countries','an advanced country technologically advanced countries such as Japan','a Christian/Muslim/Catholic etc country England became a Christian country in the seventh century.','your adopted country (= that you have chosen to live in permanently ) I felt proud of my adopted country, America.','a great country (= important, with many past achievements ) the great countries of Europe','an independent country (= not controlled by another country ) Malaysia has been an independent country since 1963.','an occupied country (= controlled by an army from another country ) For many years, Egypt was an occupied country.','a free country (= where people’s actions are not too restricted ) You can go where you like – it’s a free country.','a member country (= belonging to a particular international organization ) the member countries of the European Community','the host country (= where an event is held ) Which is the host country for the next Olympic Games?','run/govern the country (= officially control a country ) The government has the job of running the country.','rule a country (= have complete control of a country ) For a long time the country was ruled by military dictators.','leave the country The journalists were given 24 hours to leave the country.','flee the country (= leave it very quickly to avoid trouble ) At the outbreak of the war, many people fled the country.','serve your country (= work for your country in an official way ) Remember those who are serving our country as soldiers, sailors, and airmen.','lead the country She became the first woman to lead the country.','represent your country It’s a great honour to be chosen to represent your country in a sport.','betray your country (= be disloyal, especially by giving secrets to other countries ) He betrayed his country for the sake of communism.','somebody’s/something’s country of origin (= where you were born or live permanently, or where something was produced ) Please give your name, age, and country of origin.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the Scandinavian countries","translation":"کشورهای اسکاندیناوی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001682154.mp3"},{"sentence":"developing countries","translation":"کشورهای در حال توسعه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001113985.mp3"},{"sentence":"travelling to a foreign country","translation":"سفر به یک کشور خارجی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001682155.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('7d2ef3d5-4875-5ae9-96a2-fef8922d7d65','0bdffdc1-ff26-5b5d-a9a0-f5ec1243344b',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'the country','کشور؛ سرزمین؛ حومه (منطقه روستایی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('6c88d67f-c7c7-549c-8927-ce18ed42b786','0bdffdc1-ff26-5b5d-a9a0-f5ec1243344b',3,null,null,'spoken & written','an area of land that is suitable for a particular activity , has particular features , or is connected with a particular person or people','[ uncountable ]',null,'منطقه ای از زمین که برای فعالیت خاصی مناسب است، دارای ویژگی های خاصی است یا با شخص یا افراد خاصی در ارتباط است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The Peak District is good walking country.","translation":"منطقه قله یک کشور پیاده روی خوب است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001114017.mp3"},{"sentence":"mountainous country","translation":"کشور کوهستانی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001682161.mp3"},{"sentence":"the rugged moors of Brontë country","translation":"اسکله های ناهموار کشور برونته","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001682162.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('ad1ba2ab-e0ae-5ee2-92df-59c77b916aa7','0bdffdc1-ff26-5b5d-a9a0-f5ec1243344b',4,null,null,'spoken & written','country and western music','[ uncountable ]',null,'موسیقی کانتری و غربی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’m a big fan of country.","translation":"من یک طرفدار بزرگ کشور هستم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001682166.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('991df00d-738d-51fe-a692-103bd4bcbcb2','0bdffdc1-ff26-5b5d-a9a0-f5ec1243344b',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'go to the country','کشور؛ سرزمین؛ حومه (منطقه روستایی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('7731b373-a80c-575c-8c07-4c49eabb50ea','50ff249d-faca-5afb-aa33-5a4d15bd2018',1,null,null,'spoken & written','belonging to or connected with the countryside',null,null,'متعلق به روستا یا مرتبط با آن',array['rural']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"They much preferred country life to life in the city.","translation":"آنها زندگی روستایی را به زندگی در شهر ترجیح می دادند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000842714.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('7cd05800-5254-5969-8807-0d50995f4b79','50ff249d-faca-5afb-aa33-5a4d15bd2018',2,null,null,'spoken & written','relating to country and western music',null,null,'مربوط به موسیقی کانتری و غربی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a country singer","translation":"یک خواننده کانتری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001682016.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('76f5569c-2c26-58ce-b8b7-d1742a638a0f','9a14e2bf-1958-5bff-8105-a197d4722795',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the quality of being brave when you are facing a difficult or dangerous situation , or when you are very ill',null,null,'شجاعت، دلیری، جسارت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have courage She certainly has a lot of courage.','show courage The pilot showed great skill and courage.','summon (up)/muster your courage (= make yourself feel brave ) Summoning all her courage, she got up to see what the noise was.','bolster your courage (= make it stronger ) They sang and whistled as they marched, to bolster their courage.','somebody’s courage fails (= is not great enough to do something ) I was going to jump but my courage failed at the last moment.','something gives you courage (= makes you feel that you have courage ) My mother nodded, which gave me the courage to speak up.','have the courage to do something I didn’t have the courage to say what I really thought.','find the courage to do something You must find the courage to deal with the problem.','pluck up/screw up the courage to do something (= try to find it ) He was trying to pluck up the courage to end their relationship.','lack the courage to do something He lacked the courage to look her full in the face.','It takes courage to do something/sth takes courage (= needs courage ) It takes courage to make a big change in your life like that.','great courage The men had fought with great courage.','enough/sufficient courage Harry plucked up enough courage to ask her out.','personal courage (= the courage of one particular person ) Her recovery owed a great deal to her personal courage.','moral courage (= the courage to do the right thing ) He said his faith gave him the moral courage to survive his ordeal.','physical courage (= the courage to do something physically dangerous or difficult ) It seemed strange that someone of great physical courage could be so unsure of himself in other ways.','political courage (= the courage to take risks in politics ) Do our politicians have the political courage to make unpopular decisions?']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Sue showed great courage throughout her illness.","translation":"سو در طول بیماری خود شجاعت زیادی از خود نشان داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000843034.mp3"},{"sentence":"Gradually I lost the courage to speak out about anything.","translation":"کم کم جرات صحبت کردن در مورد هر چیزی را از دست دادم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001682053.mp3"},{"sentence":"He did not have the courage to tell Nicola that he was ending their affair.","translation":"او جرات نداشت به نیکولا بگوید که دارد به رابطه آنها پایان می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000384.mp3"},{"sentence":"I plucked up the courage to go out by myself.","translation":"جسارت کردم و خودم بیرون رفتم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000843038.mp3"},{"sentence":"Driving again after his accident must have taken a lot of courage (= needed courage ) .","translation":"رانندگی دوباره بعد از تصادف او باید جسارت زیادی را می طلبد (= شجاعت لازم است).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000843042.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('2ff942a1-5c49-53ec-ab9b-dde5a22838ed','9a14e2bf-1958-5bff-8105-a197d4722795',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'have the courage of your (own) convictions','شجاعت، دلیری، جسارت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have courage She certainly has a lot of courage.','show courage The pilot showed great skill and courage.','summon (up)/muster your courage (= make yourself feel brave ) Summoning all her courage, she got up to see what the noise was.','bolster your courage (= make it stronger ) They sang and whistled as they marched, to bolster their courage.','somebody’s courage fails (= is not great enough to do something ) I was going to jump but my courage failed at the last moment.','something gives you courage (= makes you feel that you have courage ) My mother nodded, which gave me the courage to speak up.','have the courage to do something I didn’t have the courage to say what I really thought.','find the courage to do something You must find the courage to deal with the problem.','pluck up/screw up the courage to do something (= try to find it ) He was trying to pluck up the courage to end their relationship.','lack the courage to do something He lacked the courage to look her full in the face.','It takes courage to do something/sth takes courage (= needs courage ) It takes courage to make a big change in your life like that.','great courage The men had fought with great courage.','enough/sufficient courage Harry plucked up enough courage to ask her out.','personal courage (= the courage of one particular person ) Her recovery owed a great deal to her personal courage.','moral courage (= the courage to do the right thing ) He said his faith gave him the moral courage to survive his ordeal.','physical courage (= the courage to do something physically dangerous or difficult ) It seemed strange that someone of great physical courage could be so unsure of himself in other ways.','political courage (= the courage to take risks in politics ) Do our politicians have the political courage to make unpopular decisions?']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('d9b6e8ac-c657-59f1-9ada-1cdb0f896b6b','61c0661f-83b9-5f50-90fb-2eac38b0c73a',1,null,null,'spoken & written','something that is crucial is extremely important, because everything else depends on it',null,null,'سرنوشت‌ساز، بسیار مهم',array['vital']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['play a crucial role/part in something Parents play a crucial role in preparing their children for adult life.','be of crucial importance Good leadership is of crucial importance in motivating staff.','absolutely crucial Technology has an absolutely crucial role in modern medicine.','prove crucial (= be crucial ) His appointment was to prove crucial to the organization’s success.','remain crucial Logging remains crucial to the country’s economy.','regard/consider something as crucial The city was regarded as crucial to the area’s defence.','a crucial factor/part/element The cost of the project is the crucial factor.','a crucial point This was a crucial point in our relationship.','a crucial question She seemed to be trying to avoid the crucial question.','a crucial issue The study of consumer behaviour is a crucial issue in marketing.','a crucial difference There is a crucial difference between the British and American attitudes.','a crucial moment/time At the crucial moment, he withdrew the support of the army.','a crucial stage The peace talks are now at a crucial stage.','a crucial decision/step Choosing a career is a crucial decision to make.','crucial information The government did not publicize this crucial information.','crucial evidence The prosecution had forgotten one piece of crucial evidence.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"This aid money is crucial to the government’s economic policies.","translation":"این پول کمک برای سیاست های اقتصادی دولت بسیار مهم است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001696446.mp3"},{"sentence":"The work of monks was crucial in spreading Christianity.","translation":"کار راهبان در گسترش مسیحیت بسیار مهم بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001696449.mp3"},{"sentence":"The city of Mycenae played a crucial role in the history of Greece.","translation":"شهر Mycenae نقش مهمی در تاریخ یونان ایفا کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001696452.mp3"},{"sentence":"The conservation of tropical forests is of crucial importance .","translation":"حفاظت از جنگل های استوایی از اهمیت حیاتی برخوردار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001696453.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('4e01f88c-b9b2-51c7-a0b9-6851fc636bd5','941634ef-5ef5-5ba2-8d0b-0ad61990ebe0',1,'in a society','در یک جامعه','spoken & written','the beliefs , way of life, art, and customs that are shared and accepted by people in a particular society','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'فرهنگ؛ کشت (میکروب)؛ کشت (زیره)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['Western/American/Japanese etc culture Our society was heavily influenced by Greek and Roman culture.','national culture Sport is a major part of our national culture.','local culture The local culture of the island has much to interest visitors.','a common culture (= one that societies or people share ) Britain and America are united by a common culture.','traditional/ancient culture The people have a traditional culture which has hardly changed in 500 years.','modern culture Computers are a part of modern culture.','the dominant culture (= the main culture in an area where there are many different cultures ) What are the values of the dominant culture?','culture shock (= the confusion or shock that people sometimes feel in a very different country or place )']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We speak Danish at home so that the boys don’t lose touch with their language and culture.","translation":"ما در خانه به زبان دانمارکی صحبت می کنیم تا پسرها ارتباط خود را با زبان و فرهنگ خود از دست ندهند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001748748.mp3"},{"sentence":"In our culture, it is rude to ask someone how much they earn.","translation":"در فرهنگ ما بی ادبی است که از کسی بپرسیم چقدر درآمد دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001748749.mp3"},{"sentence":"I love working abroad and meeting people from different cultures.","translation":"من عاشق کار در خارج از کشور و ملاقات با مردم از فرهنگ های مختلف هستم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001748750.mp3"},{"sentence":"A brief history of Western culture.","translation":"تاریخچه مختصری از فرهنگ غرب","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001122483.mp3"},{"sentence":"Business is one of the major forces in modern culture.","translation":"تجارت یکی از نیروهای اصلی در فرهنگ مدرن است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001748753.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('213a7ee9-e340-5daa-977b-1e1558a9a214','941634ef-5ef5-5ba2-8d0b-0ad61990ebe0',2,'in a group','در یک گروه','spoken & written','the attitudes and beliefs about something that are shared by a particular group of people or in a particular organization','[ countable, uncountable ]','subculture','نگرش ها و باورها در مورد چیزی که توسط گروه خاصی از مردم یا در یک سازمان خاص مشترک است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['Western/American/Japanese etc culture Our society was heavily influenced by Greek and Roman culture.','national culture Sport is a major part of our national culture.','local culture The local culture of the island has much to interest visitors.','a common culture (= one that societies or people share ) Britain and America are united by a common culture.','traditional/ancient culture The people have a traditional culture which has hardly changed in 500 years.','modern culture Computers are a part of modern culture.','the dominant culture (= the main culture in an area where there are many different cultures ) What are the values of the dominant culture?','culture shock (= the confusion or shock that people sometimes feel in a very different country or place )']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Every government department has its own particular culture.","translation":"هر بخش دولتی فرهنگ خاص خود را دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001748755.mp3"},{"sentence":"Changing the corporate culture is a long and difficult process.","translation":"تغییر فرهنگ سازمانی فرآیندی طولانی و دشوار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001748758.mp3"},{"sentence":"In the field of drug development, the culture of secrecy is deep and strong.","translation":"در زمینه توسعه دارو، فرهنگ رازداری عمیق و قوی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001748764.mp3"},{"sentence":"modern American youth culture","translation":"فرهنگ مدرن جوانان آمریکایی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001122499.mp3"},{"sentence":"the drug culture that is destroying so many young lives today","translation":"فرهنگ مواد مخدر که امروزه زندگی بسیاری از جوانان را نابود کرده است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001122498.mp3"},{"sentence":"the German political culture","translation":"فرهنگ سیاسی آلمان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001748770.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('fd8ead15-61e1-5bf0-ab90-0aef4c626298','941634ef-5ef5-5ba2-8d0b-0ad61990ebe0',3,'art/music/literature','هنر/موسیقی/ادبیات','informal','activities that are related to art, music, literature etc','[ uncountable ]',null,'فعالیت های مرتبط با هنر، موسیقی، ادبیات و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['Western/American/Japanese etc culture Our society was heavily influenced by Greek and Roman culture.','national culture Sport is a major part of our national culture.','local culture The local culture of the island has much to interest visitors.','a common culture (= one that societies or people share ) Britain and America are united by a common culture.','traditional/ancient culture The people have a traditional culture which has hardly changed in 500 years.','modern culture Computers are a part of modern culture.','the dominant culture (= the main culture in an area where there are many different cultures ) What are the values of the dominant culture?','culture shock (= the confusion or shock that people sometimes feel in a very different country or place )']::text[],'[{"sentence":"If it’s culture you’re looking for, the city has plenty of museums and art galleries.","translation":"اگر به دنبال فرهنگی هستید، این شهر دارای تعداد زیادی موزه و گالری هنری است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001122511.mp3"},{"sentence":"the Italian Ministry of Culture","translation":"وزارت فرهنگ ایتالیا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001748772.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('5fb4245f-1628-549e-8e7a-63f145c9e0b4','941634ef-5ef5-5ba2-8d0b-0ad61990ebe0',4,'society','جامعه','spoken & written','a society that existed at a particular time in history','[ countable ]',null,'جامعه ای که در زمان خاصی از تاریخ وجود داشته است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['Western/American/Japanese etc culture Our society was heavily influenced by Greek and Roman culture.','national culture Sport is a major part of our national culture.','local culture The local culture of the island has much to interest visitors.','a common culture (= one that societies or people share ) Britain and America are united by a common culture.','traditional/ancient culture The people have a traditional culture which has hardly changed in 500 years.','modern culture Computers are a part of modern culture.','the dominant culture (= the main culture in an area where there are many different cultures ) What are the values of the dominant culture?','culture shock (= the confusion or shock that people sometimes feel in a very different country or place )']::text[],'[{"sentence":"This technique was then adapted and refined by the more sophisticated cultures of the ancient world.","translation":"این تکنیک سپس توسط فرهنگ های پیچیده تر دنیای باستان اقتباس و اصلاح شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001748776.mp3"},{"sentence":"primitive cultures","translation":"فرهنگ های بدوی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001748777.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
