('d67d693c-a3c9-5b46-bdff-2e80e78c7d28','ab96b96b-dac2-5b9e-b1ad-aa7dfb2a2434',3,null,null,'spoken & written','one of the four suit s (= types of cards ) in a set of playing cards , which has the design of a red diamond shape on it','[ countable ]',null,'یکی از چهار کت و شلوار (= انواع کارت ها) در مجموعه کارت های بازی که طرحی به شکل الماس قرمز روی آن است.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the ace of diamonds","translation":"آس الماس","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985174.mp3"},{"sentence":"You have to play a diamond.","translation":"باید الماس بازی کنی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001141143.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('8519f5dd-76ee-5767-94b1-c56bff068dcc','ab96b96b-dac2-5b9e-b1ad-aa7dfb2a2434',4,null,null,'spoken & written','the area in a baseball field that is within the diamond shape formed by the four base s','[ countable ]',null,'ناحیه ای در زمین بیسبال که به شکل الماس است که توسط چهار پایه تشکیل شده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('0f4ddbbe-ac5c-5e78-8258-ccde857963cf','1c2f937c-6902-5f4f-8986-0ca25059ed74',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to talk about something with another person or a group in order to exchange ideas or decide something',null,null,'بحث کردن، گفت‌وگو کردن (برای هم‌رأی شدن)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['discuss the question/subject We’d never discussed the question of having children.','discuss the problem I suggested going out for a drink to discuss the problem.','discuss the matter/issue formal (= discuss a subject or problem ) The two leaders met to discuss the issue further.','discuss a topic (= subject of general interest ) I sometimes let the class choose which topic they want to discuss.','discuss the situation They held a three-hour meeting to discuss the situation.','discuss a possibility Government officials were seriously discussing the possibility of war.','discuss a plan/idea It’s a good idea to discuss your plans with your parents.','discuss the future of something He met the chairman of Nuclear Electric to discuss the future of the nuclear generating industry.','discuss the details Let’s get together soon to discuss the details of the trip.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Littman refused to discuss the case publicly.","translation":"لیتمن از بحث عمومی درباره این پرونده خودداری کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000803767.mp3"},{"sentence":"If you would like to discuss the matter further, please call me.","translation":"اگر مایل به بحث بیشتر در مورد موضوع هستید، لطفا با من تماس بگیرید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001830894.mp3"},{"sentence":"Pupils should be given time to discuss the book with their classmates.","translation":"باید به دانش‌آموزان فرصت داد تا درباره کتاب با همکلاسی‌های خود بحث کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000803770.mp3"},{"sentence":"Your accountant will discuss with you how to complete these forms.","translation":"حسابدار شما نحوه تکمیل این فرم ها را با شما در میان خواهد گذاشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000803773.mp3"},{"sentence":"It’s good to be able to talk about these things.","translation":"خوب است که بتوان در مورد این موارد صحبت کرد.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,5),
('88e92c49-edf9-53f1-9c4d-e5bc4e3a81ce','1c2f937c-6902-5f4f-8986-0ca25059ed74',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to talk or write about something in detail and consider different ideas or opinions about it',null,null,'صحبت کردن یا نوشتن درباره چیزی با جزئیات و در نظر گرفتن ایده ها یا نظرات مختلف در مورد آن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['discuss the question/subject We’d never discussed the question of having children.','discuss the problem I suggested going out for a drink to discuss the problem.','discuss the matter/issue formal (= discuss a subject or problem ) The two leaders met to discuss the issue further.','discuss a topic (= subject of general interest ) I sometimes let the class choose which topic they want to discuss.','discuss the situation They held a three-hour meeting to discuss the situation.','discuss a possibility Government officials were seriously discussing the possibility of war.','discuss a plan/idea It’s a good idea to discuss your plans with your parents.','discuss the future of something He met the chairman of Nuclear Electric to discuss the future of the nuclear generating industry.','discuss the details Let’s get together soon to discuss the details of the trip.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"This topic will be discussed in Chapter 4.","translation":"این موضوع در فصل 4 مورد بحث قرار خواهد گرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000803782.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('4faa73a2-4755-5277-a1cb-c6511a46a63b','c98d14ab-53e6-5bd6-8085-808565c45fe4',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an illness which affects a person, animal, or plant','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'بیماری، مرض؛ ناخوشی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a disease How long have you had the disease?','suffer from a disease About three million people suffer from the disease.','catch/get a disease ( also contract a disease formal ) He caught the disease while travelling in Africa.','develop a disease A few years ago, she developed a serious lung disease.','pass on a disease ( also transmit a disease formal ) They may pass the disease on to their children.','cause a disease Smoking is probably the major factor causing heart disease.','prevent a disease It has been claimed that fibre in the diet could help prevent many serious diseases.','treat a disease The disease can be treated with antibiotics.','cure a disease The plant was believed to cure diseases in humans and cattle.','fight (a) disease (= try to stop it continuing ) Some bacteria help the human body fight disease.','a disease spreads The government have no idea how far the disease has spread.','common common childhood diseases','rare She suffers from a rare bone disease.','serious vaccines against serious diseases like hepatitis and meningitis','fatal/deadly (= that causes death ) If left untreated, the disease can be fatal. Thousands of children are struck down by this deadly disease every year.','incurable (= that cannot be cured ) Diseases that were once thought incurable can be treated with antibiotics.','infectious/contagious (= that spreads quickly from one person to another ) The disease is highly contagious.','a skin/brain/lung etc disease The fumes have caused skin diseases among the villagers.','heart/liver/kidney disease He is being treated for kidney disease.','a hereditary/inherited disease (= that is passed from parent to child ) Parents are offered screening for some hereditary diseases.','a sexually-transmitted disease (= that is spread by having sex ) There was a worrying rise in the number of sexually-transmitted diseases.','a degenerative disease (= that gradually gets worse ) She was suffering from a degenerative disease that confined her to a wheelchair.','a chronic disease (= continuing for a long time and not possible to cure ) Chronic disease is sometimes seen as an inevitable part of being old.','a cure for a disease There is no known cure for this disease.','an outbreak of a disease (= when a disease appears in a number of people or animals ) There has been an outbreak of the disease in Wales.','the spread of a disease Knowing the facts about AIDS can prevent the spread of the disease.','the symptoms of a disease (= physical signs that someone has a disease ) To begin with, there are often no symptoms of the disease.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She suffers from a rare disease of the brain.","translation":"او از یک بیماری نادر مغزی رنج می برد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000804808.mp3"},{"sentence":"His father died of heart disease.","translation":"پدرش بر اثر بیماری قلبی درگذشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000466.mp3"},{"sentence":"She contracted the disease while she was abroad on holiday.","translation":"او زمانی که برای تعطیلات در خارج از کشور بود به این بیماری مبتلا شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001961959.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('ca078f92-cbda-571c-a0d3-498b2ac071ba','c98d14ab-53e6-5bd6-8085-808565c45fe4',2,null,null,'spoken & written','something that is seriously wrong with society or with someone’s mind, behaviour etc','[ countable ]',null,'چیزی که به شدت با جامعه یا با ذهن، رفتار و غیره کسی اشتباه است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a disease How long have you had the disease?','suffer from a disease About three million people suffer from the disease.','catch/get a disease ( also contract a disease formal ) He caught the disease while travelling in Africa.','develop a disease A few years ago, she developed a serious lung disease.','pass on a disease ( also transmit a disease formal ) They may pass the disease on to their children.','cause a disease Smoking is probably the major factor causing heart disease.','prevent a disease It has been claimed that fibre in the diet could help prevent many serious diseases.','treat a disease The disease can be treated with antibiotics.','cure a disease The plant was believed to cure diseases in humans and cattle.','fight (a) disease (= try to stop it continuing ) Some bacteria help the human body fight disease.','a disease spreads The government have no idea how far the disease has spread.','common common childhood diseases','rare She suffers from a rare bone disease.','serious vaccines against serious diseases like hepatitis and meningitis','fatal/deadly (= that causes death ) If left untreated, the disease can be fatal. Thousands of children are struck down by this deadly disease every year.','incurable (= that cannot be cured ) Diseases that were once thought incurable can be treated with antibiotics.','infectious/contagious (= that spreads quickly from one person to another ) The disease is highly contagious.','a skin/brain/lung etc disease The fumes have caused skin diseases among the villagers.','heart/liver/kidney disease He is being treated for kidney disease.','a hereditary/inherited disease (= that is passed from parent to child ) Parents are offered screening for some hereditary diseases.','a sexually-transmitted disease (= that is spread by having sex ) There was a worrying rise in the number of sexually-transmitted diseases.','a degenerative disease (= that gradually gets worse ) She was suffering from a degenerative disease that confined her to a wheelchair.','a chronic disease (= continuing for a long time and not possible to cure ) Chronic disease is sometimes seen as an inevitable part of being old.','a cure for a disease There is no known cure for this disease.','an outbreak of a disease (= when a disease appears in a number of people or animals ) There has been an outbreak of the disease in Wales.','the spread of a disease Knowing the facts about AIDS can prevent the spread of the disease.','the symptoms of a disease (= physical signs that someone has a disease ) To begin with, there are often no symptoms of the disease.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Loneliness is a disease of our urban communities.","translation":"تنهایی بیماری جوامع شهری ماست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000804817.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('aea276d1-d4f2-54f7-8cce-48881dd47a6c','1f2e8686-6346-50ca-bf32-387a4ac89ed5',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to refuse to consider someone’s idea, opinion etc, because you think it is not serious , true , or important',null,null,'رد کردن، بی‌اعتبار شمردن؛ مرخص کردن (کارمند)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['dismiss an idea/suggestion Both actors dismissed any idea of a romantic relationship between them.','dismiss a notion formal (= idea ) The Minister dismissed the notion that he had cut petrol tax because of the forthcoming by-election.','dismiss a possibility The prime minister dismissed the possibility of an early election.','dismiss a claim An industrial tribunal dismissed his claim of unfair discrimination.','dismiss an allegation/charge She claimed that she was honest and dismissed the allegations against her.','dismiss a thought Was he lying? I tried to dismiss the thought.','dismiss fears The Transport Minister dismissed fears that the Cotswold railway line would close.','dismiss criticism He dismissed criticism of the country''s human rights record.','easily/lightly (= without much thought ) This is a question that cannot be dismissed lightly.','dismiss something out of hand (= immediately, without thinking about it ) It''s an interesting idea so don''t dismiss it out of hand.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The government has dismissed criticisms that the country’s health policy is a mess.","translation":"دولت انتقادات مبنی بر اینکه سیاست بهداشتی کشور به هم ریخته است را رد کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717524.mp3"},{"sentence":"He just laughed and dismissed my proposal as unrealistic.","translation":"او فقط خندید و پیشنهاد من را غیرواقعی رد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001146215.mp3"},{"sentence":"It’s an idea that shouldn’t be dismissed out of hand (= dismissed immediately and completely ) .","translation":"این ایده‌ای است که نباید بی‌سابقه کنار گذاشته شود (= بلافاصله و به طور کامل کنار گذاشته شود).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717527.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('df401aae-7aa7-5423-b04a-0ea610f3a887','1f2e8686-6346-50ca-bf32-387a4ac89ed5',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to remove someone from their job',null,null,'برای برکناری کسی از کارش',array['fire','sack']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['dismiss an idea/suggestion Both actors dismissed any idea of a romantic relationship between them.','dismiss a notion formal (= idea ) The Minister dismissed the notion that he had cut petrol tax because of the forthcoming by-election.','dismiss a possibility The prime minister dismissed the possibility of an early election.','dismiss a claim An industrial tribunal dismissed his claim of unfair discrimination.','dismiss an allegation/charge She claimed that she was honest and dismissed the allegations against her.','dismiss a thought Was he lying? I tried to dismiss the thought.','dismiss fears The Transport Minister dismissed fears that the Cotswold railway line would close.','dismiss criticism He dismissed criticism of the country''s human rights record.','easily/lightly (= without much thought ) This is a question that cannot be dismissed lightly.','dismiss something out of hand (= immediately, without thinking about it ) It''s an interesting idea so don''t dismiss it out of hand.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Bryant was unfairly dismissed from his post.","translation":"برایانت ناعادلانه از سمت خود برکنار شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717534.mp3"},{"sentence":"Employees can be dismissed for sending obscene emails.","translation":"کارمندان را می توان به دلیل ارسال ایمیل های ناپسند اخراج کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717537.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was sacked (British English) / fired (American English) for being late all the time.","translation":"او اخراج شد (انگلیسی انگلیسی) / اخراج شد (انگلیسی آمریکایی) به دلیل اینکه همیشه دیر می آمد.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,3),
('0a21fe8a-a51f-52f6-a8fc-2c96616eb56e','1f2e8686-6346-50ca-bf32-387a4ac89ed5',3,null,null,'formal','to tell someone that they are allowed to go, or are no longer needed',null,null,'به کسی بگوید که اجازه رفتن دارد یا دیگر نیازی نیست','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['dismiss an idea/suggestion Both actors dismissed any idea of a romantic relationship between them.','dismiss a notion formal (= idea ) The Minister dismissed the notion that he had cut petrol tax because of the forthcoming by-election.','dismiss a possibility The prime minister dismissed the possibility of an early election.','dismiss a claim An industrial tribunal dismissed his claim of unfair discrimination.','dismiss an allegation/charge She claimed that she was honest and dismissed the allegations against her.','dismiss a thought Was he lying? I tried to dismiss the thought.','dismiss fears The Transport Minister dismissed fears that the Cotswold railway line would close.','dismiss criticism He dismissed criticism of the country''s human rights record.','easily/lightly (= without much thought ) This is a question that cannot be dismissed lightly.','dismiss something out of hand (= immediately, without thinking about it ) It''s an interesting idea so don''t dismiss it out of hand.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The class was dismissed early today.","translation":"کلاس امروز زود اخراج شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001146235.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('0811b84f-609e-5ed9-be15-f6b1542b546d','1f2e8686-6346-50ca-bf32-387a4ac89ed5',4,null,null,'spoken & written','if a judge dismisses a court case, he or she stops it from continuing',null,null,'اگر قاضی پرونده دادگاه را رد کند، از ادامه آن جلوگیری می کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['dismiss an idea/suggestion Both actors dismissed any idea of a romantic relationship between them.','dismiss a notion formal (= idea ) The Minister dismissed the notion that he had cut petrol tax because of the forthcoming by-election.','dismiss a possibility The prime minister dismissed the possibility of an early election.','dismiss a claim An industrial tribunal dismissed his claim of unfair discrimination.','dismiss an allegation/charge She claimed that she was honest and dismissed the allegations against her.','dismiss a thought Was he lying? I tried to dismiss the thought.','dismiss fears The Transport Minister dismissed fears that the Cotswold railway line would close.','dismiss criticism He dismissed criticism of the country''s human rights record.','easily/lightly (= without much thought ) This is a question that cannot be dismissed lightly.','dismiss something out of hand (= immediately, without thinking about it ) It''s an interesting idea so don''t dismiss it out of hand.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The case was dismissed owing to lack of evidence.","translation":"این پرونده به دلیل فقدان شواهد منتفی شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001146247.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('00b0684f-e1b3-5cb3-ad5c-9a08182d17af','1f2e8686-6346-50ca-bf32-387a4ac89ed5',5,null,null,'spoken & written','to end the innings of a player or team in the game of cricket',null,null,'برای پایان دادن به اینینگ های یک بازیکن یا تیم در بازی کریکت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['dismiss an idea/suggestion Both actors dismissed any idea of a romantic relationship between them.','dismiss a notion formal (= idea ) The Minister dismissed the notion that he had cut petrol tax because of the forthcoming by-election.','dismiss a possibility The prime minister dismissed the possibility of an early election.','dismiss a claim An industrial tribunal dismissed his claim of unfair discrimination.','dismiss an allegation/charge She claimed that she was honest and dismissed the allegations against her.','dismiss a thought Was he lying? I tried to dismiss the thought.','dismiss fears The Transport Minister dismissed fears that the Cotswold railway line would close.','dismiss criticism He dismissed criticism of the country''s human rights record.','easily/lightly (= without much thought ) This is a question that cannot be dismissed lightly.','dismiss something out of hand (= immediately, without thinking about it ) It''s an interesting idea so don''t dismiss it out of hand.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('f73efc05-bd1f-5b9e-a703-3259c5cb591b','7db441e4-1419-5800-a5d3-1884ae84e727',1,'objects','اشیاء','spoken & written','an arrangement of things for people to look at or buy',null,null,'نمایش، به‌نمایش‌گذاری؛ مانیتور؛ نمایش (ویژگی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a fine/magnificent/spectacular/dazzling display (= a very good one ) The museum has a magnificent display of silver.','a window display (= in the window of a shop ) I stopped to look at something in the window display.','a special display There was a special display of local photographs.','a floral display (= of flowers ) The village has won an award for its floral displays.','create a display She created an award-winning display at the national garden show.','a display case/cabinet (= small cupboard with a glass front ) There was a display case full of medals.','a display board Some schools have a display board with photographs of all the staff.','a display stand (= table with shelves etc used for showing things to the public ) A lot of companies had impressive display stands in the conference hall.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a superb display of African masks","translation":"نمایشی عالی از ماسک های آفریقایی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001147251.mp3"},{"sentence":"a dazzling display (= very good display ) of flowers","translation":"نمایش خیره کننده (= نمایش بسیار خوب) از گل ها","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-002084556.mp3"},{"sentence":"The window display caught her eye.","translation":"نمایشگر پنجره نظر او را جلب کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717567.mp3"},{"sentence":"display cases containing old photographs","translation":"ویترین حاوی عکس های قدیمی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717571.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('fe2c4691-2b75-5233-8f66-2b1b1ee48bde','7db441e4-1419-5800-a5d3-1884ae84e727',2,'entertainment','سرگرمی','spoken & written','a public performance of something that is intended to entertain people',null,null,'اجرای عمومی چیزی که برای سرگرم کردن مردم است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a fine/magnificent/spectacular/dazzling display (= a very good one ) The museum has a magnificent display of silver.','a window display (= in the window of a shop ) I stopped to look at something in the window display.','a special display There was a special display of local photographs.','a floral display (= of flowers ) The village has won an award for its floral displays.','create a display She created an award-winning display at the national garden show.','a display case/cabinet (= small cupboard with a glass front ) There was a display case full of medals.','a display board Some schools have a display board with photographs of all the staff.','a display stand (= table with shelves etc used for showing things to the public ) A lot of companies had impressive display stands in the conference hall.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a fireworks display","translation":"یک نمایش آتش بازی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001147259.mp3"},{"sentence":"a display of juggling","translation":"نمایش شعبده بازی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-002101851.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('6aef96dc-8eb4-5e74-9910-c17a0c2e44e1','7db441e4-1419-5800-a5d3-1884ae84e727',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'on display','نمایش، به‌نمایش‌گذاری؛ مانیتور؛ نمایش (ویژگی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a fine/magnificent/spectacular/dazzling display (= a very good one ) The museum has a magnificent display of silver.','a window display (= in the window of a shop ) I stopped to look at something in the window display.','a special display There was a special display of local photographs.','a floral display (= of flowers ) The village has won an award for its floral displays.','create a display She created an award-winning display at the national garden show.','a display case/cabinet (= small cupboard with a glass front ) There was a display case full of medals.','a display board Some schools have a display board with photographs of all the staff.','a display stand (= table with shelves etc used for showing things to the public ) A lot of companies had impressive display stands in the conference hall.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('98f8b13d-de6c-5e90-bb62-4d5afbb9eef5','7db441e4-1419-5800-a5d3-1884ae84e727',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'display of affection/emotion/aggression etc','نمایش، به‌نمایش‌گذاری؛ مانیتور؛ نمایش (ویژگی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a fine/magnificent/spectacular/dazzling display (= a very good one ) The museum has a magnificent display of silver.','a window display (= in the window of a shop ) I stopped to look at something in the window display.','a special display There was a special display of local photographs.','a floral display (= of flowers ) The village has won an award for its floral displays.','create a display She created an award-winning display at the national garden show.','a display case/cabinet (= small cupboard with a glass front ) There was a display case full of medals.','a display board Some schools have a display board with photographs of all the staff.','a display stand (= table with shelves etc used for showing things to the public ) A lot of companies had impressive display stands in the conference hall.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('4deb46ca-833b-5e49-a774-0f82717ce293','7db441e4-1419-5800-a5d3-1884ae84e727',5,'on equipment','روی تجهیزات','spoken & written','a part of a piece of equipment that shows information, for example a computer screen',null,null,'بخشی از یک تجهیزات که اطلاعات را نشان می دهد، به عنوان مثال صفحه نمایش کامپیوتر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a fine/magnificent/spectacular/dazzling display (= a very good one ) The museum has a magnificent display of silver.','a window display (= in the window of a shop ) I stopped to look at something in the window display.','a special display There was a special display of local photographs.','a floral display (= of flowers ) The village has won an award for its floral displays.','create a display She created an award-winning display at the national garden show.','a display case/cabinet (= small cupboard with a glass front ) There was a display case full of medals.','a display board Some schools have a display board with photographs of all the staff.','a display stand (= table with shelves etc used for showing things to the public ) A lot of companies had impressive display stands in the conference hall.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"This time the display flashed a red warning signal.","translation":"این بار نمایشگر یک سیگنال هشدار قرمز چشمک زد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717592.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('e3a1920a-7ef5-5644-a644-1e2627734748','acc196d3-b2b2-55d3-b46e-9292e3a9a1c1',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to show something to people, or put it in a place where people can see it easily','[ transitive ]',null,'نمایش دادن؛ به‌نمایش گذاشتن؛ برملا کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"shop windows displaying the latest fashions","translation":"ویترین مغازه ها که آخرین مدها را به نمایش می گذارد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000806549.mp3"},{"sentence":"All the exam results will be displayed on the noticeboard.","translation":"تمامی نتایج آزمون بر روی تابلوی اعلانات نمایش داده می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001975539.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('12df7701-9438-588c-abaa-63be258bc4a3','acc196d3-b2b2-55d3-b46e-9292e3a9a1c1',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to clearly show a feeling, attitude , or quality by what you do or say','[ transitive ]',null,'با آنچه انجام می دهید یا می گویید به وضوح یک احساس، نگرش یا کیفیت را نشان دهید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She displayed no emotion on the witness stand.","translation":"او هیچ احساسی در جایگاه شاهد نشان نداد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717464.mp3"},{"sentence":"ten piano pieces, each written to display the talents of individual players","translation":"ده قطعه پیانو که هر کدام برای نشان دادن استعدادهای تک تک نوازندگان نوشته شده است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000806553.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('a3e37935-7541-5a5f-9b0d-d7c2938624ec','acc196d3-b2b2-55d3-b46e-9292e3a9a1c1',3,null,null,'spoken & written','if a computer or something similar displays information, it shows it on its screen','[ transitive ]',null,'اگر رایانه یا چیزی مشابه اطلاعاتی را نمایش دهد، آن را روی صفحه نمایش خود نشان می دهد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I pressed ‘return’ and an error message was displayed.","translation":"\"بازگشت\" را فشار دادم و یک پیغام خطا نمایش داده شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000806558.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('3f672dda-da77-5c77-915b-642855cf26c8','acc196d3-b2b2-55d3-b46e-9292e3a9a1c1',4,null,null,'spoken & written','if a male bird or animal displays, it behaves in a particular way as a signal to other birds or animals, especially to attract a female','[ intransitive ]',null,'اگر یک پرنده یا حیوان نر نمایش داده شود، به شکل خاصی به عنوان سیگنالی برای پرندگان یا حیوانات دیگر رفتار می کند، به ویژه برای جذب ماده.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('8379742a-8a27-5c4d-9733-f89b3c729281','21401763-2c44-5758-8e8d-7b518212f33e',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a serious argument or disagreement',null,null,'اختلاف، منازعه؛ جدل (طولانی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['resolve/settle a dispute (= end it ) It is hoped that the dispute can be resolved peacefully.','be involved in a dispute The US government became involved in a dispute with China.','get into a dispute (= become involved ) We don’t want to get into a dispute with them.','be in dispute with somebody He was in dispute with the company about his contract.','be locked in a dispute (= be involved in one that is difficult to resolve ) Workers and management are locked in a bitter dispute.','a dispute arises (= starts ) Sometimes a dispute arises between the seller and the buyer.','a bitter/fierce dispute (= very angry ) It caused a bitter dispute between the neighbouring republics.','a long-running dispute (= continuing for a long time ) India’s long-running dispute with Pakistan','an industrial dispute British English, a labor dispute American English (= between workers and employers ) A lot of working days are lost through industrial disputes.','a pay dispute (= about how much money employees are paid ) The pay dispute involved 450 staff.','a political/legal dispute There was a long legal dispute between the two companies.','a domestic dispute formal (= between people who live together ) The court heard that he had been stabbed during a domestic dispute.','a border dispute (= about where the border between two countries is ) a border dispute between Argentina and Chile','a territorial dispute (= about which country land belongs to ) The war started as the result of a territorial dispute.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The firm is involved in a legal dispute with a rival company.","translation":"این شرکت درگیر یک اختلاف حقوقی با یک شرکت رقیب است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001962540.mp3"},{"sentence":"He got into a dispute over a taxi fare.","translation":"او بر سر کرایه تاکسی با هم اختلاف پیدا کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717622.mp3"},{"sentence":"the bitter border dispute between the countries","translation":"اختلاف مرزی تلخ بین کشورها","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717625.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
